(3740376, 520945, 74371, '<td valign="top">I still totally enjoyed this photo. I guess my photographic "eye" isn''t what it should be, from what is written in the comments here, but for an all over pleasing photo, and one that I thought better than it was ranked... to me it is still a 9<br/> <br/>Beautiful picture, Doug!</td>', 'I still totally enjoyed this photo. I guess my photographic "eye" isn''t what it should be, from what is written in the comments here, but for an all over pleasing photo, and one that I thought better than it was ranked... to me it is still a 9 Beautiful picture, Doug!', '2007-06-05 01:53:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(3740444, 521169, 28070, '<td valign="top">Just to clarify after the challenge, I didn''t cut off the flame.  It is actually the flame of the match that I brought into the frame while the shutter was open to guarantee I caught the reaction of the alcohol.  I did have some other shots that I hit the shutter just after I threw the match in.  And everyone is right I should have used the portrait orientation. Thanks for the comments everyone.<br/> <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/portfolio.php?USER_ID=28070&amp;collection_id=23302" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Out Takes</a><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-06-05 01:25:44.</i></td>', 'Just to clarify after the challenge, I didn''t cut off the flame.  It is actually the flame of the match that I brought into the frame while the shutter was open to guarantee I caught the reaction of the alcohol.  I did have some other shots that I hit the shutter just after I threw the match in.  And everyone is right I should have used the portrait orientation. Thanks for the comments everyone. Out Takes', '2007-06-05 02:22:11.000000', '2007-06-05 02:25:44.000000', 0),
